DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nCost: Fre
 e\\nAges: 0-60 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nJoin us for a free eve
 ning where children and caretakers are invited to play in a sensory-friend
 ly\, neuro-affirming environment! We encourage the whole family to attend
 \, and therapists can join as well.\nNeurodivergent Family Nights are held
  on the second Tuesday and fourth Thursday of each month from 5-7 pm (afte
 r we close to general admission)\nSpace is Limited.\nOn these nights\, we 
 dim the lights in the museum\, turn off the sounds\, and offer a limited c
 apacity of 250 guests. Staff are happy and ready to assist with providin
 g various materials\, including noise-cancelling headphones\, fidget toys
 \, sunglasses\, and weighted materials for your convenience. \nRSVP HERE
 \n*Registration is required and opens two weeks before each event. \nPlay
  Partners TBD\\n\\nMore info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events/neurodive
 rgent-family-night-3-2026-02-26/2026-08-27/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/neurodivergent-family-night-3-2026-
 02-26/2026-08-27/
