BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hunger Action Month Kickoff
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T120000
DTSTAMP:20260825T084520Z
UID:0313f2d2d9e852e1d906fc626f1f1289@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:children,play,toddler,museum,family
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nJoin us for a hands-on community se
 rvice experience with Second Harvest Food Bank of Orange County. Children
  and families will work together to sort and pack fresh produce that will 
 help support neighbors facing food insecurity throughout our community. 
 \nTime: 9am-12pm\nIncluded in museum admission. Space is limited! Book y
 our tickets now.\n\n*Members do not require a reservation.\n*Events and da
 tes are subject to change. \nAbout the play partner:\nSecond Harvest Foo
 d Bank is a nonprofit organization in Orange County.\nTheir Vision: Orange
  County with food and nutritional security for all.\nTheir Mission: In col
 laboration with our partners\, we provide dignified\, equitable and consis
 tent access to nutritious food\, creating a foundation for community healt
 h.\nTheir Value: Integrity\, accountability\, people first\, compassion\, 
 purpose driven\, stewardship \nFrequently Asked Questions\n\nWho can par
 ticipate?\nChildren and families of all ages are welcome to help pack prod
 uce alongside the Second Harvest Food Bank team.\n\nDo I need any special 
 experience?\nNo experience is needed. Second Harvest staff and volunteer
 s will provide instructions and guidance throughout the activity.\n\nWhat 
 will we be doing?\nFamilies will help sort and pack fresh produce that wil
 l be distributed to local children\, families\, and seniors experiencing f
 ood insecurity\n\nWhy is Pretend City hosting this event?\nAs part of Hun
 ger Action Month\, we&#8217\;re helping children learn that they can make 
 a positive impact in their community through acts of kindness and service
 \n\nHow does this support child development?\nChildren practice counting\,
  sorting\, teamwork\, problem-solving\, and fine motor skills while learni
 ng empathy\, generosity\, and community responsibility\n\nIs there an add
 itional cost to participate?\nNo. This activity is included with museum a
 dmission\n\nCan my child participate for only part of the event?\nYes. 
 Families are welcome to stop by anytime between 9:00 AM and 12:00 PM\n\nW
 here does the food go?\nThe packed produce will be distributed through Sec
 ond Harvest Food Bank&#8217\;s network of community partners serving famil
 ies throughout Orange County\n\nHow many families can participate?\nParti
 cipation is available on a first-come\, first-served basis while supplies 
 last.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events/hunger-action-mon
 th-kickoff/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/hunger-action-month-kickoff/
