DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: STEM\\n\\nYoung scientists and engineers are invited 
 to explore\, build\, test\, and discover through STEM presentations. Each 
 month features a new challenge designed to spark curiosity\, encourage pro
 blem-solving\, and make learning fun through play. \nTimes: 11 am &amp\;
  2:30 pm \n*Please note programming lasts 10-30 minutes. Included in muse
 um admission. Space is limited! Book your tickets now.\n*Members do not 
 require a reservation\n*Events and dates are subject to change. \nFrequen
 tly Asked Questions \nWhat age is this activity designed for?\nSTEM Up to
  the Challenge is designed for young learners and their families. \nDo I 
 need to attend the entire program?\nNo. Families are welcome to join durin
 g the scheduled program times.\n\nWhat STEM skills will children practice?
 \nChildren will explore observation\, counting\, prediction\, problem-solv
 ing\, and early engineering concepts.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.pretendc
 ity.org/events/stem-up-to-the-challenge-2/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/stem-up-to-the-challenge-2/
